    "README.txt": {
      "type": "file",
      "hidden": false,
      "author": "SOFTCOM",
      "creation": "12-7-26",
      "content": "--------------------\nLevel 3\n--------------------\n\nYou wake up on the bed in your hostel room and look at the time in your phone beside your bed. 8:47 AM. Today is your first 9AM class at IIT Ropar. 'Class jana jaruri hota hai kya?', you think to yourself and lay back down on the bed. Attendance policy is 75% anyways, you can probably skip the first 25% of the classes. But then a sudden stroke of genius hits you: why walk all the way to LHC when you can just tunnel into the campus subnets from your room no. 111 and link your hostel router directly to the classroom mainframe network to mark a proxy for yourself?. It might turn out to be easier than walking upto M4 all the way from Brahmaputra West for you.\n\nFind the first part of the password in the hostel network and the second part in the LHC network and combine it and pass it as the argument for the 'next' command to advance to the next level.\n\nUseful Commands:\n- cd\n- ls"
    }
